WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.180
Where in the brain does a function live?

2
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:06.680
Start with the map.

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.680
From the side, the cerebral cortex divides into four lobes: frontal, parietal,

4
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:13.120
temporal and occipital.

5
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.320
The brainstem and the cerebellum sit beside them.

6
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:17.920
A map names places.

7
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.360
It does not tell you what lives in each one.

8
00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:22.753
Read the map literally.

9
00:00:23.453 --> 00:00:26.193
The precentral gyrus contains primary motor cortex.

10
00:00:26.873 --> 00:00:30.453
The postcentral gyrus contains primary somatosensory cortex.

11
00:00:31.193 --> 00:00:35.473
No region here has a single function, and no function lives in a single region.

12
00:00:36.093 --> 00:00:37.373
The cortex is a mosaic.

13
00:00:38.193 --> 00:00:42.273
One atlas of healthy young adults divides each hemisphere into one hundred eighty

14
00:00:42.273 --> 00:00:44.953
areas, and borders vary between people.

15
00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:48.187
So what kind of experiment can place a function?

16
00:00:48.847 --> 00:00:49.967
The first is a lesion.

17
00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:53.747
You compare behaviour after damage with a baseline or controls.

18
00:00:54.507 --> 00:00:57.807
A deficit shows the damaged tissue contributes to the task.

19
00:00:58.127 --> 00:00:59.127
But damage spreads.

20
00:00:59.847 --> 00:01:05.147
In a 1957 report on human patients, several medial temporal structures were removed

21
00:01:05.147 --> 00:01:08.447
at once. The memory loss could not be pinned to one.

22
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.160
The second kind is a recording.

23
00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.160
Firing goes with a stimulus or a choice.

24
00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.480
That does not show the brain uses it.

25
00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:18.220
The third kind is imaging.

26
00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.360
A BOLD fMRI signal measures blood oxygenation.

27
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:27.660
In anaesthetized macaque visual cortex, it followed local field potentials better

28
00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:32.020
than spiking. An activation does not mark a region as the seat of anything.

29
00:01:33.183 --> 00:01:35.023
The fourth kind adds activity.

30
00:01:35.823 --> 00:01:38.663
Rhesus monkeys judged the direction of noisy moving dots.

31
00:01:39.503 --> 00:01:43.643
Salzman, Newsome and their colleagues applied current in area MT where neurons

32
00:01:43.643 --> 00:01:45.003
shared a preferred direction.

33
00:01:45.683 --> 00:01:50.183
In 139 experiments, stimulation had a significant effect in 89.

34
00:01:50.883 --> 00:01:54.423
In 86 of those, choices moved toward the preferred direction.

35
00:01:54.923 --> 00:01:59.743
That shows a contribution, in that task, from the stimulated neurons, not from one

36
00:01:59.743 --> 00:02:00.403
cell type. Nuzome, Nuzome, and their colleagues applied current in area MT where

37
00:02:00.403 --> 00:02:01.223
neurons shared a preferred direction.

38
00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:05.767
Here is the rule. A lesion shows contribution, not which part of the damage

39
00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:09.227
mattered. A recording shows covariation, not use.

40
00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:13.327
Imaging shows where a blood signal goes, not which neural signal.

41
00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:17.767
Stimulation shows contribution, not that the region is required.

42
00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:20.127
Claim only what the evidence licenses.
